  "notes": "Composed of ⟦{愛|あい}→愛：02370_ai⟧ (love) + {撫|ぶ} (to stroke). Refers to touching with tenderness and affection. Used in both literal and figurative contexts.\n\nUSAGE:\n- {愛撫|あいぶ}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ (verb): to caress, to fondle\n- Often appears in literary or formal writing\n- Can describe romantic/intimate touching, maternal affection, or figurative use (wind, sunlight \"caressing\")\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{優|やさ}しく→優しい：02640_yasashii⟧{愛撫|あいぶ}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to caress gently\n- {愛撫|あいぶ}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{受|う}ける→受ける：01215_ukeru⟧: to receive a caress\n- {愛撫|あいぶ}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧よう⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧: as if caressing (figurative)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{撫|な}でる→撫でる：04411_naderu⟧: to stroke, to pet — more casual and everyday\n- ⟦さする→さする：20837_sasuru⟧: to rub gently — focuses on the rubbing motion rather than affection\n- {愛|いと}おしむ: to cherish, to hold dear — emotional rather than physical",
